    rules: [
      "Tractive effort = min(starting tractive effort, power / speed, adhesion × mass on the driven axles × g); adhesion μ = 7.5/(v + 44) + 0.161 on dry rails (Curtius and Kniffler), × 0.6 wet, × 0.15 leaves, × 0.25 ice; sand × 1.6, at most dry.",
      "Running resistance per vehicle: 2.5 + k·((v + 12)/10)² N/kN (Strahl): k 0.025 coaches and loaded wagons, 0.1 empty wagons, 0.05 locomotives, 0.03 units; gradient i ‰ = i N/kN; curves 650/(r − 55) N/kN, below 300 m 500/(r − 30) (Röckl).",
      "Acceleration = (tractive effort − resistances) / (mass × mass factor); braking for a run with the service brake (G 0.3, P 0.5, R 0.6 m/s²) within the brakes and the adhesion.",
      "Full braking distance = 3.85·v² / (6.1·ψ·(1 + λ/10) + i) m (Minden formula, ψ = 1); within the adhesion of the wheels at half the speed, the magnetic track brake's share apart.",
      "Energy: at the wheel ÷ 0.85 from the contact line, plus auxiliaries, less 0.8 of the regenerative braking (AC lines take all of it, DC half); diesel ÷ 0.8 ÷ 0.36, 9.9 kWh and 2.64 kg CO₂ per litre.",
      "Coupler forces quasi-static: what the vehicles behind a coupling need, less what traction vehicles among them pull; 450 kN for a screw coupling. Run-in when braking ≈ mass of the back half × deceleration × (length / 250 m/s) / filling time (G 22 s, P 4 s).",
      "Load limit: (tractive effort at a standstill within the adhesion − the traction vehicles' own needs) / (g·(i + 4 N/kN) + 1.04 × 0.02 m/s²) per tonne; the coupling: 450 kN / the same.",
    ],
